Repair the complete Rust source below and return a corrected complete `solution.rs` using only the standard library. Preserve the public API and shown traits.

`FocusRing::new(0)` creates an empty ring at index zero. `next` and `previous` do nothing when empty. Otherwise they wrap across every index in `0..len`, including logical lengths as large as `usize::MAX`, without arithmetic overflow and without allocating storage. `set_len` changes the length, resets the index to zero when empty, and clamps an out-of-range index to the final valid index.

`UiState::navigate` changes only the page. `UiState::close_overlay` changes only the overlay. Neither operation may alter the focus ring, and navigation must preserve the overlay.

Known-bad source:
